# API endpoint abstraction

Do **not** scatter raw API URL strings in components, scripts, or feature code. Name the domain once; call sites use the name.

## App (Next.js) routes

- Canonical path map: `lib/api/appRoutes.ts` (`appApi.checklist`, `appApi.sessions`, …).
- Prefer **domain clients** under `lib/api/` (e.g. `checklistApi.ts`) that import `appApi` — UI/hooks call `fetchChecklist` / `saveChecklist`, not `fetch("/api/…")`.
- When adding a new `app/api/**/route.ts`, also add a named entry to `appApi` and a thin client helper if anything outside the route needs it.
- Route handlers stay thin; they do not redefine their own path constants for clients.

## External / third-party APIs

- Canonical URL map: `lib/api/externalEndpoints.mjs` (imported by Node scripts and re-exported from `lib/api/externalEndpoints.ts` for the app).
- Named groups by provider: `uexApi`, `scWikiApi`, `scToolsWikiApi`, …
- Fixture / sync scripts must import these names — no inline `https://api.…` literals.
- When adding or changing an external source, update **both** `externalEndpoints.mjs` and `.cursor/third-party-sources.yaml` (see `third-party-sources.mdc`).

## Why

- Path or host changes stay in one file.
- Call sites read as domain intent (`uexApi.terminals`, `appApi.checklist`), not URL shape.
- Easier to swap mocks, version prefixes, or alternate hosts later.
